Ambassador Jennifer Locetta
Alternative Representative for Special Political Affairs
New York, New York
AS DELIVERED
Thank you, Madam President, and thank you, Acting Special Coordinator Alakbarov, for your briefing.
Nearly one year ago, this Council, through Resolution 2803, endorsed President Trump’s 20-point Comprehensive Plan to End the Gaza Conflict. This is the only blueprint for a stable, safe, and prosperous Middle East.
The Board of Peace demonstrated the wisdom of this Council’s endorsement at the high-level briefing held on September 23 during high-level week. A year ago, the National Committee for the Administration of Gaza did not exist. Today, its commissioners are appointed, trained, and its staff are ready to take responsibility.
The International Stabilization Force troops are preparing to deploy. Donors have committed $18 billion, and the Board of Peace has launched a six-month, $2.45 billion program across 66 projects.
Gaza cannot afford to return to scattered efforts that have failed in the past. We urge all UN agencies, NGOs, and donors to align behind one plan.
Success, however, depends on Hamas decommissioning its weapons. Hamas committed to disarm in October 2025 and again when it accepted the Board of Peace’s roadmap. Now it must follow through without delay.
The international community must pressure Hamas to ensure that every weapon is accounted for and every tunnel and weapons depot is decommissioned or destroyed.
Nothing will be taken on trust. Objective parties must verify each and every step. Gaza cannot rebuild while Hamas retains the ability to plunge it back into violence and chaos. Hamas will have no future role in Gaza’s governance.
The Palestinian Authority also has commitments: it must end financial and ideological support for terrorism, abandon its push for unilateral recognition, and enact long-promised reforms. Any future role for the Palestinian Authority in Gaza depends on actions and results, not just claims.
We call on all Member States to wholeheartedly support the Board of Peace, the National Committee for the Administration of Gaza, and the ISF, and to use their influence to press Hamas to finally live up to its commitments.
Thank you.
